00:15:40,941 --> 00:15:43,780
there's the so-called all-in-one in-bay automatic.

243
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:48,580
Just pull in, park, and let the car wash move around you.

244
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:51,340
as water nozzles sweep across your car.

245
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:53,700
The way we developed this machine

246
00:15:53,701 --> 00:15:55,860
is we looked at how people wash their cars.

247
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:57,780
We know that when you wash your car,

248
00:15:57,860 --> 00:16:00,000
you screw up down, you go back and forth.

249
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:02,600
You want the high pressure to hit the surface of the car

250
00:16:02,601 --> 00:16:05,320
and get a cutting effect cleaning that dirt,

251
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:07,160
pushing that dirt off the car.

252
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:10,240
The way we do that is that we have a motor

253
00:16:10,241 --> 00:16:12,560
that is turning round and round.

254
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:14,620
But what happens is through the linkage,

255
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:16,320
we're able to take that high pressure

256
00:16:16,321 --> 00:16:19,720
and we're able to make motion go up and down like this

257
00:16:19,721 --> 00:16:24,520
to be able to clean the car.

258
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:27,820
The nozzles sit inside an arch or gantry,

259
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:31,660
which sizes up your car as it rinses, soaps, and dries it,

260
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,460
all in just five minutes.

261
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:38,720
On our gantry, we have four electric eyes.

262
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:42,600
These eyes are used to be able to measure the height of the vehicle,

263
00:16:42,601 --> 00:16:47,440
And that allows this boom to come down and keep a safe distance from the vehicle

264
00:16:47,441 --> 00:16:52,540
to ensure that we have good cleaning results on every square inch of the vehicle.

265
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:59,780
Not only is the in-bay automatic system fast, it requires little maintenance,

266
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:02,280
except when it comes time to clean the sludge pit.

267
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:08,440
This pit contains all the oils, greases, dirt, trash,

268
00:17:08,441 --> 00:17:13,760
and everything that's washed off of the cars and trucks and undercarriage.

269
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:17,600
This is where it all comes down to.

270
00:17:18,060 --> 00:17:23,620
The heavy solids, the soils, the dirt, grime, grease, grit,

271
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:25,780
it all goes into the sludge pit.

272
00:17:26,300 --> 00:17:28,720
Thousands of cars have accumulated dirt here.

273
00:17:29,360 --> 00:17:31,620
We have a vacuum truck that sucks it out

274
00:17:31,621 --> 00:17:35,640
and have it taken to an EPA-approved dump site.

275
00:17:35,641 --> 00:17:38,840
Like every other commercial car wash,

276
00:17:38,841 --> 00:17:42,120
the automatic all-in-one must adhere to the Federal Clean Water Act.

277
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:49,880
But there's one car washing exception, home washing.

278
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:55,080
The federal government says we can use as much water as we want.

279
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:00,280
And once we've cleaned our car, we can dump it into the storm drain.

280
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,360
Of course, that doesn't mean we should.

281
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:08,640
According to the International Car Wash Association,

282
00:18:08,641 --> 00:18:11,640
a standard garden hose that runs for 30 minutes

283
00:18:11,641 --> 00:18:14,640
puts out 150 gallons of water.

284
00:18:14,641 --> 00:18:18,640
That's three times more than a trip through the Cloister Tunnel Wash.

285
00:18:18,641 --> 00:18:22,640
And it all goes right down the storm drain.

286
00:18:22,641 --> 00:18:25,640
For some environmentally friendly home cleaning ideas,

287
00:18:25,641 --> 00:18:29,640
Victor Scalco, who is the head detailer at Mothers Waxes & Washes,

288
00:18:29,641 --> 00:18:34,640
Huntington Beach, California, has some tips.

289
00:18:34,641 --> 00:18:36,640
Let's start with an easy one.

290
00:18:36,641 --> 00:18:38,640
No dish soap.

291
00:18:38,641 --> 00:18:39,640
It has degreasers in it.

292
00:18:39,641 --> 00:18:41,640
To clean off the dishes, it'll pull the wax off the car,

293
00:18:41,641 --> 00:18:43,640
stripping your car of its wax and shortening the life

294
00:18:43,641 --> 00:18:44,640
of the paint job.

295
00:18:44,641 --> 00:18:47,640
What you want to use is a pH-balanced car wash.

296
00:18:47,641 --> 00:18:52,640
Car wash soaps contain specialty surfactants.

297
00:18:52,641 --> 00:18:55,640
These surfactants loosen the dirt from the paint surface

298
00:18:55,641 --> 00:18:58,640
and suspend these particulates in the soap suds,

299
00:18:58,641 --> 00:19:00,640
where they can be safely rinsed away

300
00:19:00,641 --> 00:19:03,640
without removing the wax.

301
00:19:03,641 --> 00:19:08,640
And remember, whatever the soap, you have to get rid of it.

302
00:19:08,641 --> 00:19:10,640
And it could end up in a river.

303
00:19:10,641 --> 00:19:15,640
Thankfully, soap manufacturers offer biodegradable alternatives.

304
00:19:15,641 --> 00:19:21,640
The surfactants of biodegradable soaps are made from chains of carbon and hydrogen molecules.

305
00:19:21,641 --> 00:19:26,640
After they are disposed of, the surfactants are flushed from the vehicle,

306
00:19:26,641 --> 00:19:32,640
then eaten by naturally occurring bacteria and converted into carbon dioxide, water, and nutrients.

307
00:19:32,641 --> 00:19:36,320
nutrients.

308
00:19:36,321 --> 00:19:38,520
Next, don't give in to the temptation

309
00:19:38,521 --> 00:19:42,820
to use any abrasive scrub washes on your car's paint.

310
00:19:42,821 --> 00:19:46,120
That's going to take off the wax and scratch the paint.

311
00:19:46,121 --> 00:19:49,660
The sponge side is better, but it's still not the best.

312
00:19:49,661 --> 00:19:50,820
You're going to want to wash your car

313
00:19:50,821 --> 00:19:53,420
with a formulated car wash mitt, something that's soft,

314
00:19:53,421 --> 00:19:54,760
that's been designed to wash your car

315
00:19:54,761 --> 00:19:56,140
finish without scratching it.

316
00:19:56,141 --> 00:19:58,200
Sponges trap dirt and particles,

317
00:19:58,201 --> 00:20:00,760
where wash mitts will let them flow freely out of the mitt

318
00:20:00,761 --> 00:20:04,000
into the wash bucket as you clean them out.

319
00:20:04,001 --> 00:20:05,960
Our next tip has to do with those white spots

320
00:20:05,961 --> 00:20:08,400
in your windows or paint.

321
00:20:08,401 --> 00:20:12,280
Those are minerals inside city water.

322
00:20:12,281 --> 00:20:15,440
Still water and vinegar takes them right off.

323
00:20:15,441 --> 00:20:17,080
The distilled vinegar and water will break that down

324
00:20:17,081 --> 00:20:20,080
without damaging any paint, chrome, or glass.

325
00:20:20,081 --> 00:20:21,720
Here's a surprising tip.

326
00:20:21,721 --> 00:20:26,120
Think twice before you use a chamois to dry your car.

327
00:20:26,121 --> 00:20:29,080
Chamois drag particles across the surface of the paint.

328
00:20:29,081 --> 00:20:30,880
as they drag across the surface of the paint.

329
00:20:30,881 --> 00:20:33,640
They're also pulling waxes off.

330
00:20:33,641 --> 00:20:37,120
Reusable microfiber drying towels work best.

331
00:20:37,121 --> 00:20:39,800
The pores in the material are tight enough to keep out dirt,

332
00:20:39,801 --> 00:20:43,240
but wide enough to absorb water.

333
00:20:43,241 --> 00:20:46,640
And they're available at most auto care stores.

334
00:20:46,641 --> 00:20:48,280
Now, if hand drying isn't your thing,

335
00:20:48,281 --> 00:20:50,200
there's hand devices like Mr. Clean's

336
00:20:50,201 --> 00:20:53,460
all-in-one auto dry car wash, handheld devices that

337
00:20:53,461 --> 00:20:54,700
attach to your garden hose.

338
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:02,080
Release the handle and the water-saving nozzle closes.

339
00:21:02,081 --> 00:21:06,080
Flip to wash and it applies soap.

340
00:21:06,081 --> 00:21:10,080
But where does the drying part come in?

341
00:21:10,081 --> 00:21:15,080
The manufacturer says a filter removes all the minerals in the water.

342
00:21:15,081 --> 00:21:18,080
Just rinse and let Mother Nature dry your car.

343
00:21:18,081 --> 00:21:21,080
No hands, no spots.

344
00:21:21,081 --> 00:21:24,080
And our final bit of advice, wax.

345
00:21:24,081 --> 00:21:28,080
If you protect your car with a good hand-applied or machine-applied wax,

346
00:21:28,081 --> 00:21:32,360
it will protect your car for longevity more than you'll ever get at a local car wash.

347
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,180
Auto Wax.

348
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:38,280
The manufacturer of some of the industry's most popular detailing products

349
00:21:38,281 --> 00:21:40,280
may have changed their name to Auto Magic,

350
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:43,620
but they haven't changed the ingredients they use.

351
00:21:44,580 --> 00:21:48,260
The same natural wax and dental floss is still found on their products today.

352
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,280
This is carnauba wax.

353
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,800
This comes from a Brazilian palm tree.

354
00:21:52,940 --> 00:21:56,240
It's a very dense, very non-water-soluble wax.

355
00:21:57,040 --> 00:22:02,820
Too brittle to use by itself, workers must melt the carnauba wax into a hot kettle of silicon and solvent,

356
00:22:04,040 --> 00:22:05,040
blending them all together.

357
00:22:06,580 --> 00:22:10,380
Then they add preservatives to preserve the wax and dye to give it color.

358
00:22:11,300 --> 00:22:17,540
Now that we've transferred everything into the large vat, it will spin for about four hours while everything's blended together.

359
00:22:17,980 --> 00:22:20,500
Then we'll have the finished product that'll be ready to be packaged.

360
00:22:20,501 --> 00:22:25,500
On a car, a layer of wax repels water and protects the paint

361
00:22:25,501 --> 00:22:27,500
against contaminants.

362
00:22:27,501 --> 00:22:30,500
It should last for about eight washes.

363
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:37,500
OK, detailer guy, thanks for the info.

